# The market's menu contribution (#207): the Acquire rows — what buying is available to $me.
#
# A market I bid in, WHOSE WINNINGS CAN PHYSICALLY REACH MY SUBJECT, whose good a valuation
# converts into a property I hold a desire in, stating which way the lot moves it. The row is
# DEDUCED along the plumbing, link by link: the market's host holds an actuator, the actuator
# is plumbed to my own pot, so opening it puts the good where I am — and only the last link,
# that the good raises this property rather than lowering it, is STATED, once, by the domain,
# because it is physics and no topology can derive it.
#
# The valuation joins through the venue's good (#198): venue -> marketFor -> source ->
# supplies -> good <- ofGood <- valuation. Property alone stopped being enough the day two
# venues priced one property in opposite directions — a fan market lowering the moisture a
# water market raises would have put BOTH directions on BOTH rows, four rows where the world
# holds two. And the walk is what makes "this auction moves MY moisture" a conclusion: an
# agent bidding in a market no valve connects to its pot is offered no row, because a
# delivery that cannot reach you is, for you, no lever at all.
#
# This branch lived in the deliberation package's menu.rq — the market's own walk, in another
# package's file. It ships from here now (#207): the rows, the venue vocabulary and the
# bidding module that carries an Acquire out are one directory, deletable together.
#
# `$me` substituted by the collector; declares no prefixes of its own — `store.query` prepends them.

SELECT DISTINCT ?means ?property ?via ?direction ?mode WHERE {
  # An agent holds TWO shapes per property — the region it wants to be in and the survival
  # envelope it must not leave — and both carry `ssn:forProperty`, so matching on that alone
  # offered every lever twice. The severity is what tells them apart, and it is also the right
  # question: a lever is worth listing because there is something the agent WANTS about that
  # property, not because the property has an edge past which its subject dies.
  #
  # DISTINCT because a region carries three property shapes now — not looked, below, above —
  # and all three are wants. Matching a severity therefore matches three times per property,
  # and every lever would be offered three times. The row is about the property; which side
  # of it is unmet is the GOAL's business, not the menu's.
  $me ag:holds ?region ; ag:actsFor ?subject .
  ?region ssn:forProperty ?property ;
          sh:property/sh:severity ag:ShouldBecome .
  $me market:bidsIn ?via .
  ?via market:marketFor ?src .
  ?src market:supplies ?good .
  ?host market:hosts ?via ;
        actuation:hasActuator ?lever .
  ?lever actuation:actuates ?subject .
  ?valuation market:ofGood ?good ;
             market:aboutProperty ?property ;
             market:direction ?direction .
  BIND(ag:Acquire AS ?means)
  BIND(deliberation:Chosen AS ?mode)
}
